# Git workflow

When finishing changes in this repo:

1. Commit with a clear message describing why.
2. Push to `origin test` — all new work is tested there first. Do not create new version tags unless the user asks.
3. Test courses use `test-loader.js` (see SETUP-GUIDE.md "Test branch"), which runs the newest `test` commit. After pushing, check `https://api.github.com/repos/KS-TMF/risecoursetranslate/commits/test` shows the new commit.
4. Only push to `main` when the user says to go live. Live courses use `@main`; after a push to main, purge `https://purge.jsdelivr.net/gh/KS-TMF/risecoursetranslate@main/risecoursetranslate.js` and confirm the CDN serves the new version.

Only skip push if the user explicitly says not to, or if there are no changes to commit.
